  "question": {
    "text": "Let a continuous and differentiable function <math><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is such that <math><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> and <math><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> have opposite signs everywhere. Then,"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math> <mrow>  <msup>   <mi>f</mi>   <mo>&#x2032;</mo>  </msup>  <mfenced>   <mi>x</mi>  </mfenced></mrow></math> is always increasing",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>  is always increasing",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced></math>  is non-decreasing",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced></math> is decreasing",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced open=\"|\" close=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced open=\"{\" close=\"\" separators=\"|\"><mtable columnalign=\"left\"><mtr><mtd><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced></mtd><mtd><mo>:</mo></mtd><mtd><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>&#8805;</mo><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mo>-</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced></mtd><mtd><mo>:</mo></mtd><mtd><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfenced></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mfenced open=\"|\" close=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced></mrow></mfenced></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced open=\"{\" close=\"\" separators=\"|\"><mtable columnalign=\"left\"><mtr><mtd><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>'</mo></msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced></mtd><mtd><mo>:</mo></mtd><mtd><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>&#8805;</mo><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>'</mo></msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced></mtd><mtd><mo>:</mo></mtd><mtd><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfenced></math><br /><br />As <math><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> and <math> <mrow> <msup> <mi>f</mi> <mo>&#8242;</mo> </msup> <mfenced> <mi>x</mi> </mfenced></mrow> </math> have opposite signs, then <math><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced></math> is negative everywhere, hence <math><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced></math> is a decreasing function."
  }
